Yes. This should be promoted from a secondary feature to **the actual product interface**.

The website is the demonstration surface. The durable product is:

> **LiveLLM is a paid, machine-readable live economic-data layer for agents. It converts messy, changing provider information into compact, timestamped, provenance-backed facts that an agent can consume before deciding where and how to spend money.**

That positioning is much stronger for the hackathon because SerpApi becomes indispensable rather than decorative.

## Where LiveLLM sits

LiteLLM already solves a different layer extremely well: unified model access, routing/fallbacks, spend tracking, budgets and gateway infrastructure across 100+ models. Its own documentation even notes that pricing data needs to be kept updated and synchronized for correct cost tracking. ([LiteLLM][1])

So don't pitch:

```text
LiveLLM vs LiteLLM
```

Pitch:

```text
              LIVE MARKET
                  │
              SerpApi
                  │
                  ▼
             LiveLLM
       economic truth layer
                  │
       ┌──────────┼───────────┐
       ▼          ▼           ▼
    LiteLLM    OpenRouter   custom router
       │          │           │
       └──────────┴───────────┘
                  │
               agent
```

**LiteLLM answers:** “How do I call/model-route/manage these providers?”

**LiveLLM answers:** “Given what is true about the market *right now*, what are these routes actually worth?”

That distinction is excellent.

