# Make the economics of the API itself explicit

This makes the product more intellectually interesting.

An agent should buy intelligence when:

```text
expected value of better decision
>
cost of intelligence
```

So LiveLLM can expose its price alongside its estimated value.

For example:

```json
{
  "resource": "llm_route_economics",
  "price_usd": 0.002,

  "decision": {
    "estimated_route_cost_before": 1.84,
    "estimated_route_cost_after": 1.17,
    "estimated_savings_usd": 0.67
  },

  "intelligence_roi": 335
}
```

Don't claim you can always know the counterfactual, but when you can calculate it this is fantastic.

It turns LiveLLM into:

> **an economic oracle agents can decide whether it is worth consulting.**

And that's actually aligned with autonomous agents.

