# I would tier the calls

Not necessarily exact production prices yet, but conceptually:

| Resource                           |                   Cost |
| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------: |
| Cached compact market snapshot     | free / extremely cheap |
| Current model facts                |                ~$0.001 |
| Workload-specific route evaluation |         ~$0.002–$0.005 |
| Full provenance/evidence bundle    |                ~$0.005 |
| Forced fresh verification          |                ~$0.01+ |

The important distinction is between:

```text
cached verified knowledge
```

and:

```text
please spend resources to establish
what is true right now
```

That second call can legitimately cost more because LiveLLM may itself incur:

```text
SerpApi search
official-source fetch
LLM extraction
validation
storage
```

You then have a natural hierarchy:

```text
L0  known current state
L1  cached evidence
L2  economic calculation
L3  fresh market verification
```

